I look at the screen and smile.
I remember that morning in January.
"Mom, I woke up early in the morning that day," I say.
"I packed my last bag."
Mother smiles and says, "Yes, and then we all went to the airport."
"Diego drove the car," I remind her.
"There was a lot of crowd at the airport," mother says.
"We stood near the gate."
"And there you hugged me tightly."
"I cried a lot that day," I admit.
Mother's eyes tear up a little.
"We all cried, Maya," she says lovingly.
"Our Lola was also very sad."
I say, "Then I said goodbye to you."
"I took my bags and went inside."
"And you came to Mumbai by plane!" mother says, smiling.
I nod in agreement.
That goodbye was truly very difficult.
But now I am very happy here.
